add(1012,'hough-threshold','Hough threshold boundary','For the explicitly stated OpenCV rule that standard Hough lines require votes strictly greater than threshold, how should h.lines(2) and the slide comment “minimum votes=3” be reconciled?',[
('They are consistent: an integer vote count must be at least 3 to exceed 2.','This follows the strict inequality and matches the reproduced API behavior.'),('They conflict: every line with exactly 2 votes must pass a strict threshold of 2.','Equality does not pass a strict greater-than rule.'),('The argument 2 selects the second detected line and has no threshold role.','The argument is passed as the voting threshold.'),('The argument fixes the output to exactly 2 lines regardless of votes.','It controls minimum support, not an exact output count.')], 'The source comment is consistent with the declared strict OpenCV threshold. A name such as minvotes must not override checked boundary semantics.',kind='code',locator='h.lines(2) and adjacent minimum-votes=3 comment.',assumptions=['Use the explicitly supplied strict standard-Hough threshold behavior, confirmed in the recorded installed version.'])
add(1003,'first-central-proof','Why first central moments vanish','For a nonempty region with u_c=m10/m00, why is μ10=Σ(u−u_c)X_uv equal to zero?',[
('Because μ10=m10−u_c m00=m10−m10=0.','The centroid definition cancels the first central moment.'),('Because every foreground coordinate u equals zero.','A translated region need not lie at the image origin.'),('Because every region has equal horizontal and vertical spread.','Zero first central moment does not require equal spreads.'),('Because μ10 equals the unnormalized area m00.','The central first moment and zeroth moment are different quantities.')], 'Centering at the weighted mean makes positive and negative coordinate deviations sum to zero.',typ='derivation',difficulty='medium',steps=['Expand the sum as ΣuX_uv−u_cΣX_uv.','Identify m10−u_c m00.','Substitute u_c=m10/m00 and cancel.'],formulas=[F_MOM,F_CENT])
